Create `src/wang.js` - the Wang tile definition and constraint-complete lookup system.

This is the core map generation system. All tile operations must be stateless given a seed.

## Tile definition

Export `TILE_DEFS` - an array of 16 tile objects, each: `{ id, edges: [N, E, S, W] }` where each edge is 0-3.

Design the 16 tiles so the set is CONSTRAINT COMPLETE: for every possible (N_required, W_required) edge pair that can appear (16 combinations of 0-3 x 0-3), at least one tile satisfies both constraints. Verify this in code.

Edge colour semantics:
- 0 = solid wall (no passage)
- 1 = narrow corridor (1 cell wide)
- 2 = standard corridor (2 cells wide)
- 3 = wide opening / room merge (3 cells wide)

Design the tile set such that:
- Tiles with edge 0 on a side have a solid wall there
- The set contains variety: some tiles are mostly room, some mostly corridor, some dead-end pockets
- Colour 0 edges are common enough to create enclosed spaces but NOT so common they dominate
- Every (N,W) pair from 0-3 x 0-3 has at least 2 candidate tiles for variety

## Layout generation

Export `buildLayout(tileId)` - returns a 2D boolean array [LAYOUT_SIZE][LAYOUT_SIZE] (true=floor, false=wall) based on the tile's edges. Use CONFIG.LAYOUT_SIZE and CONFIG.CELL_SIZE from config.js.

Logic:
- Always make a central room (radius 2 cells from centre)
- For each edge: if edge colour > 0, carve a corridor stub of width = edge_colour cells, from the room edge to the tile border
- Corridor stubs are centred on the tile mid-axis

Export `LAYOUTS` - precomputed array of layouts for all 16 tiles.

## Constraint solver

Export `getTileIndex(globalSeed, tx, ty, getTileIndexFn)` - this is recursive/memoized via a passed-in cache Map.

Better: export `createWorldGen(globalSeed)` that returns an object with:
- `getTile(tx, ty)` - returns tile index for that position, solving constraints:
  1. Look up north tile (tx, ty-1) to get its S edge
  2. Look up west tile (tx-1, ty) to get its E edge  
  3. Filter TILE_DEFS to candidates matching needN and needW (-1 = any)
  4. If no candidates: use tile 0 as fallback AND log a warning to console
  5. Pick from candidates using tilePRNG(globalSeed, tx, ty)
  6. Memoize result in internal Map
- `getLayout(tx, ty)` - returns LAYOUTS[getTile(tx, ty)]
- `clear()` - clears memo cache
- `getSeed()` - returns globalSeed

## Constraint completeness self-check

At module load time, run a check: for all 16 combinations of (needN 0-3, needW 0-3), verify at least one tile matches. If any pair has zero candidates, throw an Error listing the missing pairs. This ensures the tile set is correct before the game runs.

VERIFICATION:
- `node --input-type=module <<'EOF'
import { TILE_DEFS, LAYOUTS, createWorldGen } from './src/wang.js';
import { CONFIG } from './src/config.js';
console.log(TILE_DEFS.length === 16 ? 'tile count OK' : 'FAIL: ' + TILE_DEFS.length);
console.log(LAYOUTS.length === 16 ? 'layout count OK' : 'FAIL');
const L = LAYOUTS[0];
console.log(Array.isArray(L) && L.length === CONFIG.LAYOUT_SIZE ? 'layout shape OK' : 'FAIL');
const wg = createWorldGen(42);
const t00 = wg.getTile(0, 0);
const t10 = wg.getTile(1, 0);
const t01 = wg.getTile(0, 1);
console.log(typeof t00 === 'number' && t00 >= 0 && t00 < 16 ? 'getTile OK' : 'FAIL');
// Verify east edge of (0,0) matches west edge of (1,0)
const e00_E = TILE_DEFS[t00].edges[1];
const e10_W = TILE_DEFS[t10].edges[3];
console.log(e00_E === e10_W ? 'east-west constraint OK' : 'FAIL: ' + e00_E + ' vs ' + e10_W);
// Verify south edge of (0,0) matches north edge of (0,1)
const e00_S = TILE_DEFS[t00].edges[2];
const e01_N = TILE_DEFS[t01].edges[0];
console.log(e00_S === e01_N ? 'north-south constraint OK' : 'FAIL: ' + e00_S + ' vs ' + e01_N);
console.log('Constraint completeness check passed (no throw = OK)');
EOF`
